<h3>Pembuatan film</h3>
Produksi.
Pembuatan film.
Pengambilan gambar utama untuk film Burnt dimulai pada 23 Juli 2014. Lokasinya di New Orleans, Louisiana dan berlangsung selama dua hari. Setelah itu, pembuatan film dipindahkan ke London. Pada 2 Oktober 2014, Nick Moore memulai pekerjaan pengeditan film.
<h2>Pemasaran</h2>
Pemasaran.
Poster pertama yang menampilkan judul Burnt dirilis pada 7 Agustus 2015.
Cooper introduced a sneak peek of the film on Today Show on August 10, 2015. The Weinstein Company released the teaser trailer on August 14, 2015. On September 21, 2015, the first international trailer was released. On September 28, 2015, the first full-length trailer for the film was released by The Weinstein Company.
<h2>Peluncuran</h2>
Peluncuran.
The film was previously scheduled to release on October 2, 2015, but in July 2015, The Weinstein Company moved the release date back to October 23, 2015. The film will be released in a limited release on October 23, 2015, before being released in a wide release on October 30, 2015. However, it was then pulled from the limited release, and was re-set to October 30, 2015, nationwide.
<h2>Penerimaan</h2>
<h3>Box office</h3>
Penerimaan.
Box office.
The film will open on October 30, 2015 alongside Our Brand Is Crisis and Scouts Guide to the Zombie Apocalypse. In its opening weekend, the film is projected to gross $7–9 million from 2,900 theaters.
<h3>Respons kritis</h3>
Respons kritis.
Burnt has received generally negative reviews from critics. On Rotten Tomatoes, the film holds a rating of 32%, based on 31 reviews, with an average rating of 4.9/10. The site's critical consensus reads, "Burnt offers a few spoonfuls of compelling culinary drama, but they're lost in a watery goulash dominated by an unsavory main character and overdone clichés." On Metacritic, the film has a score of 38 out of 100, based on 12 critics, indicating "generally unfavorable reviews".
